Package: mica-docker
Version: 29.9.3-3
Source-Date-Epoch: 1794630480
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Mica OS <hi@micaos.dev>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Provides: mica-container-engine
Conflicts: mica-podman
Depends: mica-system, mica-systemd | mica-openrc (>= 0.56-mica19), nftables, libc6 (>= 2.38), libseccomp2 (>= 2.6.0)
Description: Mica OS Docker engine
 Docker 29.9.3 (dockerd and the docker CLI), docker compose 5.7.1, containerd
 2.4.2, runc 1.5.3 and tini 0.19.0 as docker-init, built from pinned upstream
 source, with /etc/docker/daemon.json: data under /mica/containers/docker,
 the local log driver and the nftables firewall backend. The podman engine of
 mica-podman conflicts.
 .
 Nothing is enabled: micad enables docker.service from the container.enabled
 setting. /usr/lib/sysctl.d/50-mica-docker.conf turns on the IP forwarding
 dockerd needs (systemd-sysctl applies it; the OpenRC script applies it
 before dockerd starts). dockerd execs nft for its firewall rules, so
 nftables is declared. mica-system provides the /mica/containers mount the
 configuration uses. The engine root /mica/containers/docker may be the
 user's own disk: docker.service requires its mount, and the OpenRC script
 refuses to start while the disk the user's fstab names there is not
 mounted, through mica-openrc's mica-fstab and mica-require-mount
 (0.56-mica19 or later).
